<small>To the chief Musician upon Neginah, <i>A Psalm</i> of David.</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> Hear my cry, O God; attend unto my prayer.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> From the end of the earth will I cry unto thee, when my heart is overwhelmed: lead me to the rock <i>that</i> is higher than I.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> For thou hast been a shelter for me, <i>and</i> a strong tower from the enemy.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> I will abide in thy tabernacle for ever: I will trust in the covert of thy wings. Selah.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> For thou, O God, hast heard my vows: thou hast given <i>me</i> the heritage of those that fear thy name.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> Thou wilt prolong the king’s life: <i>and</i> his years as many generations.<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> He shall abide before God for ever: O prepare mercy and truth, <i>which</i> may preserve him.<br />
<sup><b>8</b></sup> So will I sing praise unto thy name for ever, that I may daily perform my vows. <br />
